    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass and the exports are working correctly. Here's a summary of the changes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance module** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- **Issue**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was not exported as a named export, only in the default export\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The default export still contains these values for backwards compatibility\n\n### 2. **Evaluation toxicity metric** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- **Issue**: `toxicityMetric` function had an incorrect signature. It was receiving `references` as the second argument but treating it as `bannedTerms`, causing the references array to be interpreted as banned keywords\n- **Fix**: Updated the signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to align with the metrics API convention where all metrics accept `(outputs, references)`\n- References are now properly ignored, and default banned terms are used\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests now pass \u2713",
